---
const pillars = [
  { n: '01', label: 'Diagnose', title: 'Your financial current state', body: 'Map every naira income, spending, debts, assets and net worth in one honest, unambiguous picture.' },
  { n: '02', label: 'Secure', title: 'Your money from inflation', body: 'Understand exactly how inflation is affecting your wealth and the specific moves that stop the erosion.' },
  { n: '03', label: 'Build', title: 'A plan you can actually execute', body: 'Learn where to invest, how to evaluate opportunities and leave with a personalised action plan built on your numbers.' },
]
---
<section class="py-20 md:py-28 px-6 bg-[#0A0A0A] text-white">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-14 items-start">
      <div>
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#FFBD40] mb-5">
          <span class="h-px w-6 bg-[#FFBD40]"></span>
          What is Beat the Odds?
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-white leading-[1.1] tracking-tight mb-6">
          A live, expert-led workshop that rebuilds your entire financial structure in one day.
        </h2>
        <p class="text-white/65 leading-relaxed mb-5">
          Beat the Odds is not a motivational talk. It is a structured working session where you arrive with your real numbers and leave with a real plan, one that connects your current cash flow to your long-term wealth goals, accounts for the current economic environment and is built to survive inflation.
        </p>
        <p class="text-white/65 leading-relaxed mb-8">
          Led by Oler Oladele, CFA a securities trader with almost 20 years in Nigerian and global financial markets. This workshop applies the same discipline used at a professional level to your personal financial situation.
        </p>
        <a href="#offer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-[#FFBD40] px-6 py-3 text-sm font-bold text-black hover:brightness-95 transition">
          Join the Waitlist →
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
        {pillars.map((p) => (
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-6">
            <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
              <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-[#FFBD40] flex items-center justify-center text-black font-bold text-sm flex-shrink-0">{p.n}</div>
              <div>
                <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#FFBD40] mb-1">{p.label}</div>
                <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-white mb-2">{p.title}</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-white/55 leading-relaxed">{p.body}</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
